 From Angry Birds: The Re-Hatched Collection.
 
+### Games that are not on ReXGlue
+
+The Display, Graphics, Controller, Keyboard and mouse and Audio sections are written for ReXGlue's settings. A game on
+another runtime lists its own in `GameInfo::settings`: sections of rows made with `ChoiceRow`, `ToggleRow`, `SliderRow`,
+`ResolutionRow`, `KeyRow`, `HeadingRow` and `ParagraphRow` (`.When(key, value)` shows a row only while another setting has
+that value). The launcher writes each value to `games/<id>/<id>.toml` and every default before the first Play, so the game
+reads what the launcher shows. Each section gets a Default settings button.
+
+A PlayStation 2 game sets `source = InstallSource::kPs2Disc`, `console = "PlayStation 2"`, `disc_serial` (from SYSTEM.CNF)
+and `installed_file`. Its image is kept as `games/<id>/game/disc.iso` (a hard link on the same drive, otherwise a copy)
+with the disc's files up to `disc_file_limit` beside it. `saves_folder` keeps saves inside `games/<id>`, where updates and
+Remove game leave them; `tag` puts a region on the game's tile. Set `features.achievements = false` for a game without
+achievements. An empty `repo` means no releases yet: updates are off and their sections are hidden.
+
+Cartoon Network Racing's `launcher/project.cpp` is a full example.
+
 ### The copy's facts
 
 The install page and the About section show the copy the port was made with: version, file name, size, SHA1, MD5,
